// Industries, the stage runtime (docs/specs/phase7/industries.md 3, 5.1; P7-IN1): three chains and their 17 stage kinds with the three tiers each. Crew bands rise with the tier and never overlap (the user's Q4 decision, section 14);
// rates are kg of the main good a worker-day at skill 50, capacity is the stations' and machines' own limit a day (0: the crews alone), store_kg what the stage's own store holds, support_pm the carriers a mine needs per 1,000 hewers.
// P7-IN2: every tier above the first names its plan (blueprints/industry_tiers.jsonc) and what must stand in the stage's premises (recognise: piece, piece*N, a|b; a tier also needs every lower tier's), capacity_unpowered is what a stage with stopped machines still does,
// accident_ppm a worker-day's risk in millionths, floods the wet days that stop a pit, winter_pm the winter's share of the day, dry_days and dry_winter_pm a drying stage's rules, loss_*_pm a kiln's, bar_pm and finery_kg a finery's, container a packing stage's cask.
